+# Defensive audit sweep: access-control, 2026-10-03
+
+## Context
+Scope: route wiring and the middleware that gates it (`app/routes/index.js`,
+`app/routes/session.js`) and the handler behind `/benefits`. Trigger: first sweep on this zone;
+the registry had no row for it. No changes in the zone since the pinned upstream commit.
+
+## Delegation
+One reviewer in a fresh session, with the brief from the skill. Pre-read: `README.md`,
+`docs/audits/categories.md`. No previous reports existed; the registry was bootstrapped in this
+run.
+
+## Verification
+| Finding | Zone | Verdict | Claimed | Verified | Reservations | Proof |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| AC-1 `/benefits` reachable by any signed-in user; the handler edits other users' benefit start dates | access-control | VERIFIED REAL | High | High | none | `test/e2e/integration/benefits_access_guard_spec.js` |
+| AC-2 `isAdminUserMiddleware` redirects to `/login` instead of answering 403, revealing that the route exists | access-control | OVER-RATED | Low | Info | the route list is public through the navigation menu; nothing is revealed | not applicable |
+
+## Confirmed defects
+
+### AC-1: function-level access control missing on `/benefits` (FIXED in this change)
+- Location: `app/routes/index.js:55` and `app/routes/index.js:56`, before the fix.
+- Class: missing function-level authorization.
+- Evidence chain: (1) both routes were mounted with `isLoggedIn` only; (2) `req.body.userId`
+  flows straight into `BenefitsDAO.updateBenefits` (`app/data/benefits-dao.js:23`) with no
+  ownership check; (3) `isAdminUserMiddleware` exists in `app/routes/session.js:25` and was not
+  wired on these routes.
+- Scenario: any authenticated employee posts `userId=<colleague>&benefitStartDate=2099-01-10`
+  to `/benefits` and changes a colleague's benefits start date.
+- Fix: wire the existing `isAdmin` middleware on both routes, the pattern the codebase already
+  defines for admin-only paths. Applied in this change.
+- Reproduction and guard: `test/e2e/integration/benefits_access_guard_spec.js`, both halves.
+  `test/e2e/integration/benefits_spec.js` updated: the non-admin case now expects the redirect.
+
+## Refused or unconfirmed candidates
+- AC-2, OVER-RATED (lens: claim correctness). Informational at most; kept out of the headline
+  count and out of the registry yield.
+
+## Coverage
+Read: `app/routes/index.js`, `app/routes/session.js`, `app/routes/benefits.js`,
+`app/data/benefits-dao.js`. Skipped: every other handler under `app/routes/` and every other
+DAO under `app/data/` (other zones). Lenses applied: exploitability, claim correctness, existing
+mitigation.
